pi-c — attribution notice

Semantics, architecture and algorithms are a C translation of "pi"
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025
Mario Zechner), pinned at upstream commit
5bc1c2c0a6f07e00e8c240304182f213ab8d311f (2026-07-25) — specifically the
@earendil-works/pi-ai and @earendil-works/pi-agent-core packages: the unified
message/tool/model types, assistant-message and agent event models, the SSE
parsing approach (anthropic-messages.ts), the agent loop control flow
(agent-loop.ts), the SKILL.md progressive-disclosure format (harness/skills.ts)
and the harness tool set (harness/tools/{read,write,edit,bash}.ts) with its
ExecutionEnv contract (harness/env/nodejs.ts).

Selected implementation techniques were cross-referenced against "ESP-Claw"
(https://github.com/espressif/esp-claw, Apache License 2.0, Copyright
Espressif Systems): growable response buffering and abort-flag placement
(claw_llm_http_transport.c), provider vtable registration (claw_llm_runtime.h),
Anthropic message-conversion edge cases (claw_llm_backend_anthropic.c),
dual-source skill directories (claw_skill) and the PSRAM-first allocation
strategy. No source files were copied verbatim.

The in-process subagent module (include/pi/pi_subagent.h, src/agent/
pi_subagent.c) is original pi-c code with no upstream-pi counterpart; its
tool-surface lifecycle protocol (spawn_agent / send_input / wait_agent /
close_agent semantics, previous-status reporting, depth/concurrency wording)
was cross-referenced against the multi-agent subsystem of "Codex CLI"
(https://github.com/openai/codex, Apache License 2.0, Copyright OpenAI).
No source files were copied verbatim.

